IMPORT prelude

-- Environmental Protection and Management Act 1999 (Singapore) -- which premises need the Director-General's written permission
-- (s 6, First Schedule), the new owner's 14-day notice (s 9), dark smoke (s 11), discharges into drains and land (s 15), toxic and
-- hazardous discharges into inland water (s 17), the hazardous substances licence (s 22), the principal contractor's liability for
-- pollution from a construction site (s 35), the maximum penalties (ss 9, 15(5), 16, 17, 18, 25, 27, 28(4), 49, 67) and composition
-- (s 72).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EPMA1999.txt ("Current
-- version as at 01 Oct 2026"), with amendments to Act 15 of 2026 (in force 1 July 2026) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 7 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the duties and offences an occupier,
-- owner, trader or contractor meets, and the penalty arithmetic. Not encoded: administration (Part 2), the conditions and works
-- permits of ss 7 and 8 beyond their penalty, air impurity standards (s 12, left to regulations), the Director-General's notice
-- powers (ss 13, 18, 19, 25, 26) beyond their penalties, noise surveillance (s 28A), licences generally (Part 9), controlled works
-- clearance certificates (Part 9A), greenhouse gases (Part 10A), enforcement powers (Part 11), cost recovery (Part 12), and the
-- Second Schedule list of hazardous substances (its two columns are scrambled in the .txt deposit and were not used).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Environmental Protection and Management Act 1999 -- pollution`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `6 and First Schedule -- scheduled premises`

-- s 6(1): "A person must not occupy or use any scheduled premises specified in the First Schedule without a written permission
-- granted by the Director-General." (2): contravention is an offence (no penalty is expressly provided, so s 67 applies).
-- First Schedule: scheduled premises are any premises (a) used for listed works -- among them (i) cement works, (ii) concrete works
-- "of each batch capacity greater than 0.5 cubic metre", (iii) asphalt works, (v) chemical works, (x) petroleum works, (xiv)
-- abrasive blasting works; (b) on which there is erected "any boiler of steam generating capacity of 2,300 kilograms or more per
-- hour, incinerator or furnace burning 500 kilograms or more of solid combustible material per hour or 220 kilograms or more of
-- liquid material per hour"; or (c) used or intended to be used for storing (i) "more than 100 tonnes" of chemicals or hydrocarbons
-- which are toxic or produce toxic gases on burning or on contact with water or air, or (ii) "more than 1,000 tonnes" of chemicals
-- or hydrocarbons "with a flash point lower than 55oC".
-- Paragraph (a) lists fourteen kinds of works; the ones not named here are folded into `other listed works`. Paragraph (b) is read
-- as applying the 500 kg / 220 kg rates to an incinerator or a furnace alike.
DECLARE Works IS ONE OF
    `cement works`
    `concrete works`
    `asphalt works`
    `chemical works`
    `petroleum works`
    `abrasive blasting works`
    `other listed works`
    `no listed works`

DECLARE Premises HAS
    `the works carried on` IS A Works
    `concrete batch capacity in cubic metres` IS A NUMBER
    `boiler steam capacity in kg per hour` IS A NUMBER
    `solid material burned in kg per hour` IS A NUMBER
    `liquid material burned in kg per hour` IS A NUMBER
    `toxic chemicals stored in tonnes` IS A NUMBER
    `low flash point chemicals stored in tonnes` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the works make the premises scheduled` IF
    CONSIDER `the premises`'s `the works carried on`
    WHEN `no listed works` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `concrete works` THEN `the premises`'s `concrete batch capacity in cubic metres` GREATER THAN 0.5
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premises are scheduled premises` IF
        `the works make the premises scheduled` `the premises`
    OR  `the premises`'s `boiler steam capacity in kg per hour` AT LEAST 2300
    OR  `the premises`'s `solid material burned in kg per hour` AT LEAST 500
    OR  `the premises`'s `liquid material burned in kg per hour` AT LEAST 220
    OR  `the premises`'s `toxic chemicals stored in tonnes` GREATER THAN 100
    OR  `the premises`'s `low flash point chemicals stored in tonnes` GREATER THAN 1000

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises, `has written permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the premises is an offence` IF
    `the premises are scheduled premises` `the premises` AND (NOT `has written permission`)

§§ `9 -- change of owner or occupier`

-- s 9(1): the new owner or occupier of scheduled premises "must notify the Director-General in writing of such change within
-- 14 days from the date the person becomes the owner or occupier"; (2) fine not exceeding $5,000.
GIVEN `days after becoming owner or occupier` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change was notified in time` IF
    `days after becoming owner or occupier` AT MOST 14

§§ `11 -- dark smoke`

-- s 11(1): any owner or occupier of industrial or trade premises "who causes, permits or allows the emission of dark smoke from a
-- chimney" of those premises is guilty of an offence. (2): not an emission "lasting for not longer than any periods that may be
-- prescribed and subject to any prescribed limitations". "Dark smoke" is smoke ascertained by a prescribed method (s 2).
GIVEN `owner or occupier of industrial or trade premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused or allowed dark smoke from a chimney` IS A BOOLEAN, `within the prescribed periods and limitations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dark smoke is an offence` IF
        `owner or occupier of industrial or trade premises`
    AND `caused or allowed dark smoke from a chimney`
    AND (NOT `within the prescribed periods and limitations`)

§§ `15 -- discharges into drains and land`

-- s 15(1): any person who discharges, or causes or permits to be discharged, "any trade effluent, oil, chemical, sewage or other
-- polluting matters into any drain or land, without a written permission" commits an offence. (6): the section "does not apply to
-- the discharge of a toxic substance or hazardous substance to which section 17 applies".
-- (2): where matter has been discharged from premises, the occupier, "other than a principal contractor to which section 35
-- applies", is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have discharged it.
-- (3): anyone who causes or suffers such matter to enter a drain or land without permission "(whether wilfully or by accident)"
-- must immediately inform the Director-General; (4) waivable where the amount is, in the Director-General's opinion, "not of a
-- substantial nature"; (5) fine not exceeding $5,000.
GIVEN `discharged into a drain or land` IS A BOOLEAN, `has written permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `section 17 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discharge is an offence under section 15` IF
        `discharged into a drain or land`
    AND (NOT `has written permission`)
    AND (NOT `section 17 applies`)

GIVEN `discharged from the occupier's premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier is a principal contractor under section 35` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier proved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier is taken to have discharged` IF
        `discharged from the occupier's premises`
    AND (NOT `the occupier is a principal contractor under section 35`)
    AND (NOT `the occupier proved otherwise`)

GIVEN `matter entered a drain or land without permission` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Director-General waived it` IS A BOOLEAN, `informed the Director-General immediately` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to inform is an offence` IF
        `matter entered a drain or land without permission`
    AND (NOT `the Director-General waived it`)
    AND (NOT `informed the Director-General immediately`)

§§ `17 -- toxic or hazardous substances in inland water`

-- s 17(1): discharging a toxic or hazardous substance "into any inland water so as to be likely to cause pollution of the
-- environment" is an offence. (5)(a): a person is deemed to discharge if the person places the substance where it is liable "to
-- fall or descend or be washed or to percolate or be blown into the water"; (b) the discharge is deemed to cause pollution if it
-- subjects "persons or animals to a material risk of death, injury or impairment of health" or threatens to pollute any inland
-- water; (c) that the substance is in containers does not of itself exclude pollution.
-- (6): "No prosecution may be instituted under this section without the written consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `discharged into inland water` IS A BOOLEAN, `placed where liable to reach the water` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is taken to have discharged into inland water` IF
    `discharged into inland water` OR `placed where liable to reach the water`

GIVEN `material risk to persons or animals` IS A BOOLEAN, `threatens to pollute inland water` IS A BOOLEAN, `the substance is in containers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discharge is taken to cause pollution` IF
    `material risk to persons or animals` OR `threatens to pollute inland water`

GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution under section 17 may be instituted` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor consented in writing`

§§ `22 -- hazardous substances licence`

-- s 22(1): a person must not "import, manufacture, possess for sale, sell or offer for sale any hazardous substance unless the
-- person holds a licence". (2): a licence "is not transferable" and authorises no individual "other than the individual named in
-- the licence". Offence (3); penalty under s 27.
GIVEN `deals in a hazardous substance` IS A BOOLEAN, `a licence is held` IS A BOOLEAN, `the dealer is named in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dealing is an offence under section 22` IF
        `deals in a hazardous substance`
    AND (NOT (`a licence is held` AND `the dealer is named in the licence`))

§§ `35 -- principal contractor of a construction site`

-- s 35(1): a principal contractor in control of a construction site "must not permit any person to commit an offence specified
-- under section 14, 15 or 17". (2): on a contravention at the site the principal contractor is presumed, until the contrary is
-- proved, (a) to have had control, (b) to have had knowledge and (c) to have permitted it. (3): presumptions (b) and (c) "are not
-- rebutted unless the defendant proves that the defendant had exercised due diligence"; (4) not due diligence "unless the
-- defendant had taken all reasonable measures ... including all the measures prescribed". (6): same punishment as for s 14, 15
-- or 17.
GIVEN `a section 14, 15 or 17 contravention at the site` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no control of the site` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable measures` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all prescribed measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the principal contractor is liable` IF
        `a section 14, 15 or 17 contravention at the site`
    AND (NOT `proved no control of the site`)
    AND (NOT (`took all reasonable measures` AND `took all prescribed measures`))

§§ `Penalties -- ss 9, 15(5), 16, 17, 18, 25, 27, 28(4), 49 and 67`

-- s 67(1): an offence (except under Part 7) with no express penalty: first conviction, fine not exceeding $20,000 and $1,000 a day
-- for a continuing offence; second or subsequent, $50,000 and $2,000 a day. No imprisonment.
-- s 27: a Part 7 offence with no express penalty: fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment up to 2 years or both, and $2,000 a day.
-- s 9(2), s 15(5): fine not exceeding $5,000. s 18(2), s 25(3): fine not exceeding $50,000.
-- s 16(3): first, $20,000 or 3 months or both, $1,000 a day; second, $50,000 or 3 months or both, $2,000 a day.
-- s 17(1): first, $50,000 or 12 months or both; second or subsequent, "both imprisonment for a term of not less than one month and
-- not more than 12 months and a fine not exceeding $100,000".
-- s 49: obstruction, $20,000 or 3 months or both; second or subsequent, $50,000 or 3 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `using scheduled premises without permission`
    `failing to notify a change of owner or occupier`
    `emitting dark smoke`
    `discharging into a drain or land without permission`
    `failing to inform of a discharge`
    `failing to treat trade effluent`
    `discharging toxic substances into inland water`
    `failing to clean up when required`
    `dealing in hazardous substances without a licence`
    `storing hazardous substances unsafely`
    `failing to remove hazardous substances when required`
    `obstructing an officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general penalty applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using scheduled premises without permission` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `emitting dark smoke` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `discharging into a drain or land without permission` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to notify a change of owner or occupier` THEN 5000
    WHEN `failing to inform of a discharge` THEN 5000
    WHEN `failing to clean up when required` THEN 50000
    WHEN `failing to remove hazardous substances when required` THEN 50000
    WHEN `dealing in hazardous substances without a licence` THEN 50000
    WHEN `storing hazardous substances unsafely` THEN 50000
    WHEN `discharging toxic substances into inland water` THEN IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000
    OTHERWISE IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 50000 ELSE 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `dealing in hazardous substances without a licence` THEN 2000
    WHEN `storing hazardous substances unsafely` THEN 2000
    WHEN `failing to treat trade effluent` THEN IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000
    OTHERWISE IF `the general penalty applies` `the offence` THEN (IF `a repeat conviction` THEN 2000 ELSE 1000) ELSE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    `the base maximum fine` `the offence` `a repeat conviction`
    PLUS `the daily fine for a continuing offence` `the offence` `a repeat conviction` TIMES `days continued after conviction`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `discharging toxic substances into inland water` THEN 12
    WHEN `dealing in hazardous substances without a licence` THEN 24
    WHEN `storing hazardous substances unsafely` THEN 24
    WHEN `failing to treat trade effluent` THEN 3
    WHEN `obstructing an officer` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is mandatory` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `discharging toxic substances into inland water` THEN `a repeat conviction`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `28(4) -- ignoring a noise stop-work order`

-- s 28(4): failing to comply with a stop-work notice under s 28(3) -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000 for every day during which the
-- notice is not complied with or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 months or to both".
GIVEN `days not complied with` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for ignoring a stop-work order` MEANS
    10000 TIMES `days not complied with`

§§ `72 -- composition`

-- s 72(1): a prescribed compoundable offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of
-- the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence" and (b) "$15,000". (2): on payment no further proceedings, but compensation,
-- damages, fees, costs and expenses remain payable.
-- The continuing daily fine is not counted in "the maximum fine that is prescribed" here; that reading is an inference.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `a repeat conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most it may be compounded for` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the base maximum fine` `the offence` `a repeat conviction` DIVIDED BY 2) 15000
